#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0223 expect=skipped domain=ADAE
#note "Data that WOULD fire if the rule ran. The AVAL column would make the heuristic say BASIC DATA STRUCTURE, but the DECLARED structure=OCCDS wins (Fix #154, carrier = the mandatory #library line), so the dataset is outside Data_Structures: [BASIC DATA STRUCTURE, MEDICAL DEVICE BASIC DATA STRUCTURE] and the rule never executes. THIS IS THE BATCH'S SINGLE GENERAL PIN on that Scope block, shared verbatim by PMDA-AD0247, PMDA-AD0582, PMDA-AD0225 and PMDA-AD0252-D - not duplicated on those rules. Worked precedent: cdisc/CDISC-AD0261-invalid-ADAE-declaration-wins-over-columns.cdt."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADAE structure=OCCDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col AEDECOD type=Char
col AVAL    type=Num
col BASE    type=Num
col CHG     type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | HEADACHE | 10 | 4 | 5
